{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"cswr.hds.harvard.edu/History.txt"},"lines":{"text":"A generous gift to Harvard Divinity School (HDS) from a group of anonymous donors brought the Center for the Study of World Religions into being. The 1957 gift was intended to \"help Harvard University maintain graduate and undergraduate courses in the religions of the world, to train teachers in this field, to give ministers a sympathetic appreciation of other religions, and to stimulate undergraduate interest in the religions of the world.\"\n"},"line_number":9,"absolute_offset":484,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"HDS"},"start":44,"end":47}]}}
